.TH CTPOOL_FUTURE_FULFILL 3 "2026-09-21" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_future_fulfill \- deliver a result to a detached future
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

ccol_retval_t ctpool_future_fulfill(ctpool_future *f, void *result);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Delivers result to a future made by ctpool_future_create_detached,
wakes every caller blocked in ctpool_future_get, and then releases the
producer's reference.

The call frees the future when that is the last reference left, which
happens when the caller has already released its own with
ctpool_future_free and no ctpool_future_get call is in progress.

Call it exactly once for each detached future. Don't call it on a
future that ctpool_submit_future, ctpool_try_submit_future or
ctpool_timed_submit_future returned: the worker thread that runs the
task of such a future fulfills it inside the library.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
f        Future handle. ctpool_future_create_detached must have made
         it, and nothing must have fulfilled it yet
result   Result value to deliver. ctpool_future_get reads it back
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        result was delivered
ccol_invalid_args   f is NULL
ccol_not_permitted  f was already fulfilled
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_future_create_detached (3),
.BR ctpool_future_get (3),
.BR ctpool_future_done (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
